Top-level script code is one span however many procedures sit between
its pieces: a top-level :TRY before a procedure and a top-level :ERROR
handler after it meet, so mixed_error_handling_families fires on the
:ERROR. The procedure in between uses neither family
(diag.mixed_error_handling_families second Flags fence).
Suspected issue: #328 — the message says the families "are mixed in the same procedure" although this span is top-level script code (diag.mixed_error_handling_families: "all top-level script code is one further span").
-- input.ssl --
:DECLARE nCount;
:TRY;
	nCount := 1;
:CATCH;
	nCount := 0;
:ENDTRY;

:PROCEDURE Helper;
	:RETURN 2;
:ENDPROC;

:ERROR;
nCount := -1;
:RESUME;
-- format --
:DECLARE nCount;
:TRY;
	nCount := 1;
:CATCH;
	nCount := 0;
:ENDTRY;

:PROCEDURE Helper;
	:RETURN 2;
:ENDPROC;

:ERROR;
	nCount := -1;
:RESUME;
-- diagnostics --
12:1-12:7 warning deprecated_keyword: ':ERROR' is legacy error handling. Prefer ':TRY' / ':CATCH' / ':FINALLY'
12:1-12:7 warning mixed_error_handling_families: Legacy ':ERROR'/':RESUME' and structured ':TRY'/':CATCH' are mixed in the same procedure - the legacy handler can intercept errors before ':CATCH' sees them; use one family per procedure
14:1-14:8 warning deprecated_keyword: ':RESUME' is legacy error handling. Prefer ':TRY' / ':CATCH' / ':FINALLY'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
12:1-12:7 warning deprecated_keyword: ':ERROR' is legacy error handling. Prefer ':TRY' / ':CATCH' / ':FINALLY'
12:1-12:7 warning mixed_error_handling_families: Legacy ':ERROR'/':RESUME' and structured ':TRY'/':CATCH' are mixed in the same procedure - the legacy handler can intercept errors before ':CATCH' sees them; use one family per procedure
14:1-14:8 warning deprecated_keyword: ':RESUME' is legacy error handling. Prefer ':TRY' / ':CATCH' / ':FINALLY'
